# Artifact JSONL files are UTF-8 text (Hebrew). Keep them diff-friendly and never
# munge line endings — the build reads them byte-for-byte.
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf

# Everything else the runner hashes or executes must check out with the SAME bytes
# on Windows. Uncovered, core.autocrlf=true made these CRLF in the worktree: that
# broke ci/runtime-lock/sefaria.txt against its committed sha256 and made every
# `.sh` unrunnable under bash (`set: pipefail\r: invalid option name`) — five
# phantom local failures against blobs that were correct all along. The blobs are
# already LF (`git ls-files --eol` reports i/lf for every file matched here), so
# this renormalises nothing and moves no fingerprint component; it fixes only what
# a Windows checkout writes.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf
*.patch text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.conf  text eol=lf

# The packed release artifact is binary (produced by the driver / CI, not committed raw).
*.zst   binary
